XPath (XML Path Language) is used to navigate through elements and attributes in an XML document. Axes methods in XPath allow you to select nodes relative to the current node. Here's a summary of the most commonly used XPath axes methods with examples:\par
\par
1)//tagname --> all elements which contain that tag name\par
2)//tagname[text()='value] --> give which element contain that text\par
3)//tagname[@AN='value'] --> which element contain that attribute\par
4)//tagname[contains(text(),'value')] -->that sub text\par
5//tagname[contains(@AN,'value')] -->we can also use and/or operator\par
6(//tagname[text/attribute])[position]\par
\par
7)//tag[starts-with(@at,'value')] -->find dynamic webelement we give starting text\par
  \b\fs24 ex:id=name12344 //span[starts-with(text(),'Women's ')] \b0\fs22\par
\par
\b ---\fs24 Axes Methods\fs22 ---\b0\par
\par
8)PARENT:\par
     select the parent of the current node\par
     //tagName[@av='value']//parent::tagname  \par
  ex://div[starts-with(@id,'desktop-grid-2')]//parent::div\par
    \par
9)CHILD:\par
      select all children of the current node\par
      //tagName[@av='value']//child::tagname  \par
   ex://select[@id='day-select']//child::*\par
      //div[@class='scheduler-suggestions']/child::button[5]\par
     \par
10)SELF:\par
     select the current node\par
     //tagName[@av='value']//self::tagname  \par
  ex://select[@id='day-select']//self::select\par
\par
11)DESCENDANT:\par
      it selects all of the descendant(children,grandchildren)current node\par
     //tagName[@av='value']//descendant::tagname\par
\par
12)DESCENDANT-OR-SELF:\par
      it select the current node and all of its descendants if tagname for descendant and self are same\par
     //tagName[@av='value']//descendant-or-self::tagname\par
 \par
 13)ANCESTOR:\par
     it selects all of the ancestors(parent,granparent)of cuurent node\par
\tab  //tagName[@av='value']//ancestor::tagname\par
\tab  //span[text()='Female']//ancestor::div\par
\tab  \par
14)ANCESTOR-OR-SELF:\par
     it selects current node and all of its ancestors if tagname of ancestor and self are same\tab  \par
\tab  //tagName[@av='value']//ancestor-or-self::tagname\par
\tab  //span[text()='Female']//ancestor-or-self::div\par
\tab  \par
15)FOLLOWING: \par
      it select all the nodes that appear after the current node\par
       //tagName[@av='value']//following::tagname\par
\tab    //span[text()='Widgets']//following::div\par
\tab   \par
16)FOLLOWING-SIBLING:\par
      it selects all the nodes that have the same parent as the current node and appear after current node  \par
\tab   //tagName[@av='value']//following-sibling::tagname\par
\tab   //a[@class='sc-jqUVSM jAsVOe active']//following-sibling::a\par
\tab  \par
17)PRECEDING:\par
      it select all the nodes that appear before the cuurent node\tab  \par
      //tagName[@av='value']//preceding::tagname\par
      //a[@class='sc-jqUVSM jAsVOe active']//preceding::a[2]\par
18)PRECEDING-SIBLING:\par
      it select all the nodes that have the same parent as current mode and appear before the current node\par
       //tagName[@av='value']//preceding-sibling::tagname\par
       //a[@href='/table']/preceding-sibling::a\par
